# vLLM v0.26.0 patch 02/18 (apply after the four DeepSeek-V4 patches above it).
#
# DeepSeek-V4 on ROCm: batch-invariant, graph-safe sparse decode.
#
# Decode tokens keep the decode metadata (full graph capture) but run the
# prefill sparse-attention kernel, the prefill indexer score kernel and the
# prefill top-k selector on capacity-sized per-request workspaces, with
# context-independent KV rows and linear indexer logits. Adds
# VLLM_DS4_DECODE_KERNEL.
#
# Why BI needs it: the paged split-K flash-decode picks its split count from the
# batch, so a decode token differed from the same token computed in a prefill
# (and from the trainer, which runs the prefill kernels).
#
# Upstream: not yet proposed. vLLM main rewrote the ROCm DeepSeek-V4 attention
# after v0.26.0 with no batch-invariant gating; this needs an RFC with the
# DeepSeek-V4 ROCm owners.
#
# Source commits:
#   [ROCm][DSv4] Batch-invariant, graph-safe sparse decode (VLLM_DS4_DECODE_KERNEL=sparse)
#   [ROCm][DSv4] Sparse decode: context-independent KV rows, linear indexer logits
#
